    "created_at": "2024-05-13T16:58:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-05-13T16:58:27Z",
    "body": "I'm wondering if content-visibility is a good concept to build on for this throttling; since the goal is similar: minimize rendering cost of content not *relevant* to the user (as opposed to just visible). For example, IIUC c-v will force layout for find-in-page. I'm wondering if lifecycle updates should similarly be resumed for offscreen iframes when the user triggers find-in-page, it's possible that a DOM update (which populates the content the user is searching for) is blocked on the next rAF.\r\n\r\n@vmpstr might have input based on edge cases like this addressed for c-v.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2108232093/reactions",
